.TH JANUSGATED 8 "August 2026" "JanusGate 0.1.2" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
janusgated \- run the JanusGate policy and packet-processing service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B janusgated
.br
.B janusgated --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B janusgated
loads persistent appliance state, publishes an immutable policy snapshot,
starts the native packet workers, and serves the authenticated local
management protocol.
It cooperates with
.BR janusgate-netd (8)
for privileged network changes and never performs those changes directly.
.PP
The service is intended to run under the supplied init definition as the
dedicated
.B janusgate
identity.
Command-line runtime tuning is deliberately not supported; persistent state
is validated before it is used.
.SH LOGGING
The service emits structured JSON records to the configured stderr and syslog
destinations.
Production defaults to the
.B info
level.
Authenticated runtime controls provide bounded per-component debug and trace
levels with mandatory expiration, rate limiting, and identifier redaction.
Use
.BR janusgatectl (1)
to inspect or change them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Display build version information and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Request an orderly stop.
.TP
.B SIGINT
Request an orderly stop.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/janusgate/janusgate.db
Persistent SQLite appliance state.
.TP
.I /var/lib/janusgate/totp.key
Private appliance-local TOTP protection key.
.TP
.I /var/lib/janusgate/backups/
Private backup archives.
.TP
.I /etc/janusgate/certs/server.pem
Combined server certificate and private key.
.TP
.I /run/janusgate/control/control.sock
Authenticated local control and management socket on Linux.
.TP
.I /run/janusgate/netd.sock
Privileged network-helper socket on Linux.
.TP
.I /var/run/janusgate/control/control.sock
Authenticated local control and management socket on OpenBSD.
.TP
.I /var/run/janusgate/netd.sock
Privileged network-helper socket on OpenBSD.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The service stopped cleanly or version information was displayed.
.TP
.B 1
Initialization, runtime, or shutdown failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH SECURITY
Do not run the service as root.
The supplied service definition restricts filesystem access, capabilities,
system calls, address families, and writable paths.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR janusgatectl (1),
.BR janusgate-netd (8),
.BR janusgate-web (8),
.BR janusgate-setup (8)
